{"duration_api_ms":1620445,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b3582635-083d-4d21-a877-4ec6aedfc636","total_cost_usd":49.05465199999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":144,"cache_creation_input_tokens":165787,"cache_read_input_tokens":35140305,"output_tokens":79209,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":27667},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":165787,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3437,"cache_read_input_tokens":579465,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1443,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1443},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":444,"outputTokens":158544,"thinkingTokens":50822,"cacheReadInputTokens":78684504,"cacheCreationInputTokens":574658,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":49.05465199999998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":113,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"All three route picks are implemented. `dart analyze lib test` exits 0 with no errors or warnings (the same 36 info-level lints in untouched files), and `flutter test` passes 79/79. The Kotlin changes are not compiled or run here, so the Android channel still needs your CI build and the phone test.\n\n## R1 — Android local player reads through the system grant\n\n**What I verified about playback without copying:**\n- The media_kit fork in use sends `Media.uri` straight to mpv's `loadfile` (`real.dart:436-438`). The Dart side has no `content://` handling. The helper's Java `openFileDescriptorJava` exists, but nothing in Dart calls it.\n- I downloaded the libmpv jar the build pins (`default-arm64-v8a.jar`, 20260906; its SHA-256 matched the build script) and searched `libmpv.so`. It contains the `fd://` and `fdclose://` stream protocols (\"Invalid FD\", \"Failed querying FD size\"). It contains no `content://` handling. The probe files are deleted.\n- So the video plays as `fdclose://<fd>`, with the fd opened by Kotlin (`openFileDescriptor(uri, \"r\").detachFd()`), and mpv closes it itself. The player asks for a fresh fd on every open (`pl_player/controller.dart`), because each open uses one up.\n\n**What I verified about the file picker:** `android_file_picker` 2.0.0's `openFileStream` always copies the whole file into `cache/file_picker`, even with the SAF options. File mode therefore uses its own `ACTION_OPEN_DOCUMENT` instead.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **Kotlin** (`MainActivity.kt`, `librepili/media` channel): new methods `pickVideoFile`, `pickVideoFolder`, `listTree`, `copyDocuments` and `openFd`. Folder and file picks take a persistable read grant; it keeps at most 100 and releases the oldest. Listing and copying run off the UI thread.\n- **New `lib/services/local_documents.dart` (166 lines):**\n  - The channel wrapper.\n  - A pure `match()` that finds the folder's video (the largest one, as on desktop) and its side files: `librepili.json`, `cover.jpg`, `<base>.danmaku.xml` or `<base>.xml`, `<base>.*.srt`, `<base>.comments.json`, and `comments_images/` when comments exist.\n- **`LocalPlayer` on Android, folder mode:**\n  - Copies only the side files into `<cache>/local_documents/<md5(key)>/`. The existing loaders find them there unchanged, because they look next to `mergedPath` / `entryDirPath`.\n  - That cache is wiped on the next open, not when the player closes.\n- **`LocalPlayer` on Android, file mode:** plays the file by URI with no copy. It then shows a one-line hint that on Android, \"打开视频文件夹\" is what loads danmaku, subtitles and comments.\n- **Resume position:** keyed by `u` + md5 of provider + document id, which stays the same when the same file is picked again.\n- **Desktop and iOS:** unchanged. Folders the app itself created still play by path from the download list.\n- **Tests:** 4 in `test/utils/local_documents_test.dart` (72 lines).\n\n## R2 — multi-segment merges no longer fall back for fixable causes\n\n- **MP4 segments with different codec configurations:** each distinct `stsd` entry is kept, and each chunk's `stsc` index points at its own entry. A segment that returns to an earlier configuration reuses that entry. A different audio sample rate (media timescale) is also converted rather than refused.\n- **FLV configuration changes** (mid-stream or between segments): one sample entry per distinct configuration.\n- **HEVC in FLV:** I added it rather than rule it out.\n  - Download durl streams are, as far as I know, always H.264. But I can't prove from the code that a durl response will never carry HEVC.\n  - Both conventions are supported: the legacy codec id 12 (common with Chinese CDNs, including Bilibili live), and enhanced FLV with the `hvc1` FourCC (frame types SequenceStart / CodedFrames / CodedFramesX).\n  - HEVC entries carry no picture size (0×0); the decoder reads the size from the SPS.\n- **Damaged segments:**\n  - Before joining, each segment is checked: its size against the byte count in `index.json`, and its structure via a new `Mp4Remuxer.checkSegment` (a cut-off FLV tag, or MP4 samples past the end of the file).\n  - Bad or missing segments are downloaded again, at most 2 rounds.\n  - If data is still damaged after that, the merge fails with the streams kept, instead of saving separate parts.\n- **Still kept as separate parts** (`UnsupportedError`):\n  - FLV codecs other than H.264/HEVC video and AAC audio.\n  - Enhanced-FLV `av01` / `vp09` / multitrack packets.\n  - A codec change between segments, e.g. `avc1` → `hvc1`. FFmpeg's MP4 demuxer switches configurations but not codecs within one track.\n  - Segments whose set of tracks differs, e.g. one segment has no audio.\n  - A mix of FLV and MP4 segments.\n- **Tests:** 11 new ones in `flv_demux_test.dart`. The old \"differing configuration is not joined\" test was replaced by one expecting the join with two sample entries.\n\n## R3 — export folders vs internal folders\n\n- **The naming rule:** `DownloadService.exportFolderName` adds \" (视频)\" to any export name matching `^(s_)?\\d+$`, compared case-insensitively because Windows folder names are case-insensitive. No internal folder can be named like the result. 3 tests in `export_folder_name_test.dart` (36 lines).\n- **The other direction:** internal page folders only ever hold entry folders.\n  - Before creating one, a same-named folder with files at its top level is moved aside to \"<id> (视频)\", and any download whose `mergedPath` pointed into it is updated.\n  - This only happens if the folder holds no downloads yet.\n- **Deletion:** a page folder that is also an export folder now loses only its download subfolders; the export files stay.\n\n## Diff summary\n\nThe cumulative working-tree diff (pass 2, the refinement and these route picks) is 36 tracked files, +1587/−280.\n\n**This turn's changes:**\n\n| File | What |\n|---|---|\n| `MainActivity.kt` | +213: the new channel methods |\n| `local_player.dart` | Android routing through the grant |\n| `pl_player/controller.dart` | `content://` → `fdclose://` |\n| `data_source.dart` | New `uri` field on `FileSource` |\n| `bili_download_entry_info.dart` | Transient `playUri` / `playKey` |\n| `video/controller.dart` | Resume key and `uri` passed to the player |\n| `mp4_remux.dart`, `mp4_join.dart`, `flv_demux.dart` | Multi-entry `stsd`, HEVC, `checkSegment` |\n| `download_service.dart` | Segment repair, naming rule, folder guards |\n| `flv_demux_test.dart` | New and updated remux tests |\n\n**New files:**\n- `lib/services/local_documents.dart` (166 lines)\n- `test/utils/local_documents_test.dart` (72 lines)\n- `test/utils/export_folder_name_test.dart` (36 lines)\n\nThe test files are gitignored and need force-adding.\n\n## Uncertainties\n\n- **R1:**\n  - Seeking through an fd depends on the content provider handing back a real, seekable file. ExternalStorageProvider and MediaProvider do; exotic providers (cloud drives) may not.\n  - If the fd can't be opened, a toast appears but the player still reports as initialised.\n  - The `video/*` filter may hide `.flv` / `.ts` files that a provider labels `application/octet-stream`.\n  - A large `comments_images/` folder is copied in full.\n- **R2:**\n  - Tests check the output structure, not real decoding. Playback of a configuration switch relies on FFmpeg's new-extradata handling.\n  - The re-download reuses the stored URLs, which can expire (roughly 2 hours). It is also cancelled if another download starts during the merge. Either way the merge then fails with the streams kept.\n  - I narrowed `_exportType1` back to catching only `UnsupportedError`, which undoes part of pass-2 F11: damaged data now fails the merge instead of splitting into parts. I believe that's what you asked for.\n- **R3:**\n  - The suffix text \" (视频)\" is my choice.\n  - A folder is moved aside only when the app creates a new download, and a user folder with files that happens to be named like an avid is moved too.\n- **Kotlin:** it relies on `startActivityForResult` / `onActivityResult` from `FlutterActivity` (via `AudioServiceActivity`), and I found no warnings-as-errors setting in the Android build.\n\n```\nTEST RESULTS:\n  runner: flutter test (+ dart analyze lib test)\n  command: source \".../scratchpad/tools/local_env.sh\" && cd \"$REPO\" && dart analyze lib test && flutter test\n  exit_code: 0\n  total: 79\n  passed: 79\n  failed: 0\n  skipped: 0\n  duration_ms: ~63000 (analyze + test)\n\nINFRA REPAIRS (during auto-repair, empty if none):\n\nREAL FAILURES (audit-fix-caused regressions, empty if none):\n\nINFRA-PERSISTENT (failures that hit the 3-cycle repair cap, empty if none):\n\nOVERALL: PASS\n```\n\nThe Gmail, Google Calendar and Google Drive connectors still need authorizing in claude.ai connector settings, and `agentbridge` still fails to connect. None of them were needed here.","ttft_ms":8574,"type":"result","duration_ms":1187417,"uuid":"4f9da347-d40f-402b-901c-822e7a7ae9f1","ttft_stream_ms":8353,"time_to_request_ms":609,"first_content_frame_ms":8354,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
